From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thingino Project <thingino@thingino.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 21:20:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] t41: keep day bank in bright daylight

The recovered bright-day BCSH bank produces neon green/cyan rendering on the
Wyze Cam v4 after its IR-cut GPIO order is corrected.  A live same-frame A/B
with the ordinary day bank removes the false color while preserving the T41
security policy's bounded AWB and low-light transitions.

Continue collecting bright-day evidence, but retain the ordinary day color
model when it saturates.  Low-light selection remains unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Thingino Project <thingino@thingino.com>
---
 src/openimp_tuning.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/openimp_tuning.c b/src/openimp_tuning.c
index d074cc6..33d48de 100644
--- a/src/openimp_tuning.c
+++ b/src/openimp_tuning.c
@@ -517,6 +517,6 @@ static int tuning_feedback(OpenIMPTuningController *controller)
         if (controller->bright_day_evidence >=
             T41_SECURITY_BRIGHT_DAY_SAMPLES) {
-            color_model = T41_COLOR_MODEL_BRIGHT_DAY;
+            color_model = T41_COLOR_MODEL_DAY;
         } else if (controller->low_light_evidence >=
                    T41_SECURITY_LOW_LIGHT_SAMPLES) {
             color_model = T41_COLOR_MODEL_LOW_LIGHT;
-- 
